ading from CDN"],[491,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[493,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1155,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[259,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[299,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[773,"`Enter/Space`"],[342,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[565,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[308,"`Escape`"],[693,"`Escape`"],[775,"`Escape`"],[1344,"`Escape`"],[378,"`FieldGroup` is purely presentational — it renders the styled `Group` and holds no React Aria context. The surrounding field wires value, disabled, and validation state into its controls."],[379,"`FieldGroup` rounds its outer corners from DOM order: the group's CSS rounds the start corners of its **first child** and the end corners of its **last child**, so controls are seamless inside and rounded only at the box edges. Author children in visual order and the rounding follows — no per-control positioning prop. A lone control (a TextField input, a Select trigger) is both first and last, so it rounds both edges. The rules are RTL-safe (they use logical `start`/`end` corners)."],[375,"`FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, and `FieldError` each render `null` when they have no content, so callers pass `label` / `description` / `errorMessage` straight through without guarding."],[410,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1617,"`Flex` is a one-dimension